WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:02.690
Hey, Josh and Craig.
嗨，乔什和克雷格。

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:03.570
My name is Heather.
我叫海瑟。

3
00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:05.250
I am from Clearfield, Utah.
我来自犹他州克利尔菲尔德。

4
00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.430
What does How About Your Mother mean to me?
《老爸老妈浪漫史》对意味着什么？

5
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:08.910
I absolutely love the show.
我真的超级喜欢这部剧。

6
00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.410
I've watched every season several times,
每一季我都刷了好几遍，

7
00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:16.670
but I'm actually sending this voice note to you guys
但其实我给你们发这条语音消息

8
00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:20.510
because I just listened to the episode that you did
是因为我刚刚听了你们制作的那期节目，

9
00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:24.550
about how you guys spent your summers between seasons two and three.
关于你们在第二季和第三季之间的夏天是怎么度过的。

10
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:31.290
And I know what you went through, Craig, with your son.
克雷格，我懂你经历过什么，关于你的儿子。

11
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.830
I had my son actually 14 weeks early.
其实我儿子早产了整整14周。

12
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.430
He spent five months in the hospital.
他在医院住了五个月。

13
00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.450
He was weighing one pound, ten ounces when he was born.
他出生时只有一磅十盎司重。

14
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:47.810
There was plenty of times where we did not know if my son was going to make it home.
有很多次我们都不知道我儿子能不能活着回家。

15
00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:57.030
And listening to that episode, it makes me realize that there's other people out there that don't.
听了那一集，让我意识到还有其他人……

16
00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:04.930
Sorry, that go through this kind of stuff that me and Craig have gone through.
抱歉，是经历过我和克雷格所经历这种事的人。

17
00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:12.690
And I appreciate you for being vulnerable in that podcast episode, Craig.
克雷格，我很感激你在那一期播客里展现出脆弱的一面。

18
00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.670
I know this is supposed to be 60 seconds.
我知道这应该控制在60秒内。

19
00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:15.150
I'm sorry.
对不起。

20
00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:15.810
I'm going over.
我超时了。

21
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:21.110
I just want to let you guys know that now my son is 13 years old.
我只是想让你们知道，现在我儿子13岁了。

22
00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:25.070
He has become completely obsessed with Marilyn Monroe.
他变得对玛丽莲·梦露完全着迷。

23
00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:26.810
He says he's going to marry her one day.
他说他有一天要娶她。

24
00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.110
Fingers crossed.
祝一切顺利吧。

25
00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:35.670
He can name all the presidents that we've ever had from George Washington to where we're at now.
他能说出我们历任所有总统的名字，从乔治·华盛顿到现在的每一位。

26
00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:43.970
He is an amazing kid and I just wanted to thank you guys and let you know that this podcast really helps
他是个令人惊叹的孩子，我只是想谢谢你们，让你们知道这个播客真的很有帮助，

27
00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.350
and it really means a lot to a lot of people out there.
对外面很多很多人来说意义重大。

28
00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:47.970
Thank you so much.
非常感谢你们。

29
00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.920
Hello, welcome back to How We Made Your Mother.
哈喽，欢迎回到《我们是如何创造你母亲的》。

30
00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:12.840
I'm Josh Radner.
我是乔什·拉德纳。

31
00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.220
I'm here with Craig Thomas.
我和克雷格·托马斯在一起。

32
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.480
Hey, Josh.
嘿，乔什。

33
00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:22.580
Craig co-created this show, How I Met Your Mother, that I was on for a long time.
克雷格共同创作了这部我演了很久的剧《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

34
00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.520
And we've been doing this podcast for a while now.
而且我们做这个播客也有一段时间了。

35
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.840
And man, how are you feeling hearing that, Craig?
天哪，听到这个你有什么感觉，克雷格？

36
00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.120
Just blown away.
简直震撼。

37
00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:31.960
Just blown away.
简直震撼。

38
00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:43.480
I almost can't even talk about how much it means to me that, you know, you try to talk about the stuff you go through.
我几乎说不出这对我有多大意义，你知道的，当你试着谈论你经历的事情时。

39
00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:48.680
We had these lives we were living while we were making this TV show and all this stuff is happening
我们在制作这部电视剧的同时过着自己的生活，所有这些事情都在发生，

40
00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.180
and not all of it went on the TV show.
而且并非所有事情都上了电视剧。

41
00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:56.140
Of course, it informed the TV show, but not all of it makes it on the TV show.
当然，它为电视剧提供了灵感，但并非所有事都能进入电视剧。

42
00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:02.120
So to have this opportunity with this podcast to talk about what was going on in our human lives
所以通过这个播客，有机会谈论在我们人类生活中发生的事情，

43
00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:10.580
outside of the lives we're creating on TV, you know, it's always vulnerable to share those very real things we've been through.
在我们在电视上创造的生活之外，你知道的，分享我们经历过的那些非常真实的事情总是需要勇气的。

44
00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:19.580
But to know that it hit this, you know, that it speaks to people out there and we get a message like that, it's incredibly meaningful.
但知道它击中了这一点，你知道，它能触动外面的听众，我们能收到这样的信息，真的非常有意义。

45
00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.160
Thank you for that beautiful message.
谢谢你发来这么美好的信息。

46
00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:26.260
I'm so happy to hear your son is 13 years old and doing amazing.
听到你儿子13岁了而且过得很好，我太高兴了。

47
00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:30.940
And, like, what you've been through, not everybody in your life understands it.
而且，就像你经历过的那样，你生活中的并不是每个人都能理解。

48
00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.620
There's no way they could.
他们根本不可能理解。

49
00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.400
You kind of don't know what that one's like unless you go through it.
除非你亲自经历过，否则你根本不知道那种感觉是什么样的。

50
00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.400
And it feels very, very lonely.
而且感觉非常、非常的孤独。

51
00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.820
And I felt very lonely in that moment of my life.
在我生命中的那个时刻，我感到非常孤独。

52
00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.480
And making this TV show made me feel less lonely.
而制作这部电视剧让我感到不那么孤独了。

53
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:53.080
The idea that the show found you and then its podcast found you and that, you know, that it speaks to people and finds people out there.
这部剧找到了你，然后它的播客也找到了你，你知道的，它能与人们对话并在人群中找到彼此，这种想法……

54
00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.020
I think things find people, right?
我觉得事物会找到属于它的人，对吧？

55
00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:58.500
You put these things out there and you just believe in your heart it's going to find people.
你把这些东西创作出来，并且你内心深信它会找到那些需要它的人。

56
00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.540
So thank you for letting me know that that found you and sharing your story with us.
所以谢谢你让我知道它找到了你，并与我们分享你的故事。

57
00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.460
I just can't tell you how much it means to me.
我简直无法形容这对我的意义有多重大。

58
00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:15.240
Craig, I'm struck by just the simple act of being truthful and vulnerable, like the consequential kind of downstream effects of that, which are so beautiful.
克雷格，我被这种坦诚和脆弱的纯粹行为深深打动了，比如它随之带来的那些美妙的后续影响。

59
00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:24.140
And I heard this thing once that said, when we talk about our accomplishments, it breeds competition and sometimes envy.
我曾经听过这样一句话，当我们在谈论各自的成就时，它会滋生竞争，有时还有嫉妒。

60
00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:28.780
But when we are vulnerable, it breeds community.
但当我们展现脆弱时，它会滋生社群感。

61
00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:29.620
Yeah.
对。

62
00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:30.420
Yeah.
对。

63
00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:33.700
You know, we find each other at our wounds, right?
你知道的，我们在彼此的伤口处认出对方，对吧？

64
00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:34.960
At the places we're hurting.
在我们痛苦的地方。

65
00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:36.540
Yeah, that's right.
是的，没、错。

66
00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:41.180
And I'm glad, I'm so glad we did that episode.
我很高兴，我非常高兴我们做了那一期节目。

67
00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:48.180
And I'm so glad that the podcast is meeting people where they, just as How I Met Your Mother did.
我也非常高兴这个播客能在人们所在的地方陪伴他们，就像《老爸老妈浪漫史》曾经做的那样。

68
00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:54.340
I mean, there's a kind of, this is a cousin of the show or so, you know, it's kind of a, it's a companion of the show.
我的意思是，这有点像，这是这部剧的表亲之类的，你知道的，它有点像这部剧的同伴。

69
00:04:54.340 --> 00:05:02.520
And I hope, my hope is that some of what people consider so magical and heartwarming and loneliness,
我希望，我的希望是人们认为的那种神奇、温馨且能排解孤独的东西——

70
00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:08.800
