那是个不可能完成的任务。

285
00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:30.720
And somehow with the guidance of Pamela Fryman, we accomplished it.
但不知怎么的，在帕梅拉·弗莱曼的指导下，我们完成了。

286
00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:33.000
And you, I mean, also.
还有你，我是说，也有你的功劳。

287
00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:34.040
Too humble, too humble.
太谦虚了，太谦虚了。

288
00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:38.440
With Zuzi Greenberg too, you guys were hashing things out all the time.
还有苏琪·格林伯格，你们俩当时一直在反复商量。

289
00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:40.980
And I had never worked with either one of them.
而且我以前从未跟他们俩任何一个人合作过。

290
00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:46.520
I mean, Zuzi, the wonderful story is, if you haven't heard it, Zuzi called me and said,
我是说，苏琪，有个美妙的故事，如果你还没听过的话，苏琪打电话给我说，

291
00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:47.840
hey, do you have a moment for Pam?
嘿，你有空跟帕姆聊聊吗？

292
00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:50.420
And I'm like, I've met Pam once briefly.
我说，我只简短地见过帕姆一次。

293
00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:51.640
And I said, sure.
然后我说，当然。

294
00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:53.520
She called me.
她给我打了电话。

295
00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:55.280
Zuzi called me.
苏琪给我打了电话。

296
00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:57.520
I spoke to Pam for about 10, 15 minutes.
我和帕姆聊了大约10、15分钟。

297
00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:00.340
And then Zuzi called me and said, show up Monday.
然后苏琪又打电话给我说，周一直接来上班。

298
00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:02.200
Michael, I forgot.
迈克尔，我给忘了。

299
00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:04.240
I'm ashamed I forgot the backstory of this too.
我很羞愧，我也把这背后的故事给忘了。

300
00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:06.280
But like, did you know Zuzi?
但是，你之前认识苏琪吗？

301
00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:10.340
How did you, like if you hadn't worked with either one of them, which I kind of forgot.
你是怎么——如果你之前没有跟他们俩任何一个人合作过，这事我其实有点忘了。

302
00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.040
Because my God, you guys became such a team.
因为天哪，你们俩配合得简直就像个黄金组合。

303
00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:14.480
It's almost hard to conceive of.
几乎让人难以想象。

304
00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.080
That was the first time you guys ever worked together.
那是你们俩第一次合作。

305
00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.040
But how did you get in the mix?
但你是怎么加入进来的呢？

306
00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:18.350
I had never worked with Zuzi.
我以前从未和祖兹合作过。

307
00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:23.540
I had never, a friend of mine said no to the job and said that I was available.
我从来没有，我有个朋友推掉了这份工作，然后说我有空。

308
00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:24.660
That was it.
就是这样。

309
00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:25.160
See?
看吧？

310
00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:26.740
That's how a lot of life happens.
生活很多时候就是这样发生的。

311
00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:28.240
I've completely forgotten that part.
我把那部分完全忘了。

312
00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:30.360
Is that 21 years ago, I think?
那是21年前吗，我想？

313
00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:30.880
Yeah.
对。

314
00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:35.780
So, Michael, where were you, what have you worked on before How I Met Your Mother?
所以，迈克尔，你在哪里，在《老爸老妈浪漫史》之前你都做过些什么？

315
00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:36.760
Like, remind me.
比如，提醒我一下。

316
00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.480
I know, did you do Boy Meets World?
我知道，你演过《男孩成长记》吗？

317
00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:39.460
I did.
我演过。

318
00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:40.560
I did.
我演过。

319
00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:42.980
I did start on Boy Meets World.
我确实是从《男孩成长记》开始的。

320
00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.020
I go all the way back to Married with Children.
我甚至能追溯到《奉子成婚》的时候。

321
00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:47.440
I mean, we did some home improvement.
我的意思是，我们做过一些《家居装饰》。

322
00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:49.300
I did all those sitcoMs.
我拍过所有那些情景喜剧。

323
00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:50.120
As a first?
作为第一导演？

324
00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:51.180
No, no.
不，不。

325
00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:52.040
Not as a firSt.
不是作为第一导演。

326
00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:55.920
I hadn't done too many Run of the House with Joey Lawrence.
我跟乔伊·劳伦斯拍过《左右为难》，不算太多。

327
00:15:55.920 --> 00:16:00.980
I had done as a first, a couple of episodes of different shows.
作为第一导演，我拍过几集不同的节目。

328
00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:05.480
But I had done a pilot that was much like How I Met Your Mother was written.
但我拍过一部试播集，它的写作风格跟《老爸老妈浪漫史》非常像。

329
00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:06.200
Okay.
好吧。

330
00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:09.020
So, coming off that pilot, I got a lot of time.
所以，拍完那部试播集后，我有了很多时间。

331
00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:11.040
Like, a lot of scenes, a lot of cuts, a lot of flashbacks.
比如，大量的场景，大量的转切，大量的闪回。

332
00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:12.500
So, they were like, this guy can juggle.
所以他们就觉得，这家伙能应付得来。

333
00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:15.760
I mean, Michael, you did not know what you were getting yourself into, though, signing
我的意思是，迈克尔，不过当你签约《老爸老妈浪漫史》的时候，

334
00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:16.500
up for How I Met Your Mother.
你根本不知道自己将要面对什么。

335
00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:19.820
We were throwing, like, 80-scene, 20-minute episodes at you.
我们把诸如80个场景、20分钟长度的剧集一股脑儿全扔给你。

336
00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:26.560
Imagine the task of scheduling a three-day shoot for 75 scenes, like, which you had to
想象一下，为75个场景安排为期三天的拍摄任务有多难，比如，你不得不

337
00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:27.940
do over and over and over again.
一遍又一遍、一遍又一遍地那么做。

338
00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:30.480
When you would get one of those episodes, you'd see it coming down the pike.
每当你拿到其中某一集时，你就会看到它迎面扑来。

339
00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:33.600
Was that exciting for you, or was that like, oh, my God?
这对你来说是让人兴奋，还是觉得天哪，不会吧？

340
00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:34.420
Did you hate us?
你讨厌我们吗？

341
00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:36.860
No, it was an oh, my God task every week.
不，每周都是一个“天哪”级别的任务。

342
00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:37.800
I mean, I would...
我的意思是，我会……

343
00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:42.620
But, you know, when we were shooting it, it was an oh, my God, this is amazing.
但是，你知道，当我们拍摄时，那种感觉是天哪，这也太棒了。

344
00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:43.080
Really.
真的。

345
00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:43.360
Yeah.
对。

346
00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:43.900
It really was.
真的就是这样。

347
00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:47.040
Well, you seemed undaunted at every turn, Michael.
好吧，迈克尔，你每到一个转折点都显得毫不畏惧。

348
00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:48.960
Were you actually daunted and panicked?
你当时其实感到害怕和惊慌了吗？

349
00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:52.840
Because you could not have presented calmer and chiller.
因为你当时表现得不可能再冷静、再淡定了。

350
00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:53.840
Were you deep?
你内心其实波涛汹涌吗？

351
00:16:53.980 --> 00:16:56.120
But inside your own head, you never seemed like you're panicking.
但你在自己脑海里，看起来从来没有恐慌过。

352
00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:56.820
Were you...
你当时……

353
00:16:56.820 --> 00:17:00.600
Did you ever get one and you were like, these guys are fucking certifiably insane.
你有没有过这种感觉，觉得这群人简直特么是疯了。

354
00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:01.660
How will this happen?
这会怎么发生呢？

355
00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:03.480
When Kobe...
当科比……

356
00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:08.220
Was it on the back lot and jumping the cars?
是在后景地块上跳跃汽车吗？

357
00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:09.960
I'm not sure what episode that was.
我不确定那是哪一集了。

358
00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:10.440
Oh, we just did that.
哦，我们刚拍过那个。

359
00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:12.560
The jumping with the bike?
骑单车跳跃？

360
00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:14.280
Yeah, that was the one right before this.
对，就是紧挨着这一集之前的那一集。

361
00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:15.280
But you had the bike jump.
但你当时有单车飞跃的戏。

362
00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:15.900
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

363
00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:16.300
I heart New Jersey.
我爱新泽西。

364
00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:18.960
And Pam would explain it.
然后帕姆会解释。

365
00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:22.060
Pam would explain it like, this is what's going to happen.
帕姆会这样解释：接下来会发生这些事。

366
00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.000
We're going to do this.
我们要这么做。

367
00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:27.740
I'm in just an awe of Pam LaFryman and her ability to put things together.
我简直对帕姆·拉弗莱曼以及她统筹全局的能力佩服得五体投地。

368
00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.720
And really, for nine seasons, that's what I did.
真的，整整九季，我都是这么过来的。

369
00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:32.560
I just was in awe of her.
我就是对她佩服得五体投地。

370
00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:34.820
So let me ask you this, Michael.
那我问你个问题，迈克尔。

371
00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:35.960
This is just a broader question.
这是一个更宏观的问题。

372
00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:38.820
From episode one to 200 and episode 208,
从第一集到第200集以及第208集，

373
00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.300
what did you learn about making television?
你从制作电视剧中学到了什么？

374
00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:43.140
And what did you learn specifically from Pam?
你具体从帕姆身上学到了什么？

375
00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:47.380
Well, I really learned from Pam how to run a set.
嗯，我真的从帕姆身上学到了如何掌控剧组。

376
00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:53.680
And like you guys said, to do it calmly and to do it politely and respect everybody on the set.
就像你们说的，要保持冷静、礼貌，并且尊重剧组里的每个人。

377
00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:58.500
And it's not easy because you come from the school of roughness when you're an AD.
这不容易，因为如果你当过副导演，你是从那种严厉的作风里出来的。

378
00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:00.140
You got it right.
你说得对。

379
00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:01.160
You're moving people around.
你在调度人员。

380
00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:02.440
You can't always be...
你不能总是……

381
00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:03.260
Yeah, you're moving people around.
对，你在指挥着大家。

382
00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:05.100
You don't have to be necessarily polite.
你未必要对人客客气气的。

383
00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:06.940
But Pam set a tone.
但帕姆定下了基调。

384
00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:13.260
I always remember set a tone of just respecting every single department.
我一直记得要定下这样一个基调：尊重每一个部门。

385
00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:13.700
Yeah.
对。

386
00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:17.320
So I would have to say that's the biggest thing I carry with me.
所以我要说这是我随身携带的最大收获。

387
00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:17.840
Yeah.
对。

388
00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:24.660
And that respect, I think what it did was everyone felt a certain amount of dignity on the set in whatever role they were in.
而且这种尊重，我认为它的作用是让每个人在剧组里都感受到一定程度的尊严，无论他们扮演什么角色。

389
00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:27.840
So they were bringing their A game every person.
所以每个人都拿出了最好的状态。

390
00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:28.480
Yeah.
对。

391
00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:30.360
We wanted to work for Pam.
我们都愿意为帕姆工作。

392
00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:30.980
Yeah.
对。

393
00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:33.260
Chris LaFontaine, our director of photography.
克里斯·拉方丹，我们的摄影指导。

394
00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:36.640
I mean, he would come to me as like whatever she needs, you know.
我的意思是，他会跑来跟我说，只要她需要什么，你知道的。

395
00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:36.940
Yeah.
对。

396
00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:38.980
And the whole crew was that way.
整个剧组都是这样的。

397
00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:39.380
Yeah.
对。

398
00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:42.660
So that's the biggest thing I think I learned from...
所以这是我认为我从……学到的最大东西。

399
00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:44.040
It elevates everything, right?
这提升了一切，对吧？

400
00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:48.540
Because everyone's that much more invested and they feel valued because they are valuable.
因为每个人都投入更多，而且他们感到了自己的价值，因为他们的确很有价值。

401
00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:50.820
And they know that they are part of the final product.
而且他们知道自己是最终成品的一部分。

402
00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:52.040
And like, Michael, that is it.
而且，迈克尔，就是这样。

403
00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:58.760
Like, we would write these crazy scripts, but they're just going to be words on a page that are insane unless they can be made real.
比如，我们会写出那些疯狂的剧本，但如果它们不能变成现实，就只是一页纸上荒谬的文字。

404
00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:00.020
And you guys made them real.
而你们把它们变成了现实。

405
00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:05.000
And you were a big part of the weekly manifestation of the madness coming out of Reddit.
而且你是每周将Reddit上的疯狂创意具象化的重要推手。

406
00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:05.700
And I'll tell you this, Michael.
而且我告诉你，迈克尔。

407
00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:09.720
The five of us were not the ruliest bunch.
我们这五个人可不是最守规矩的一群人。

408
00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:12.060
Is that where guys, guys, guys comes in?
那就是“伙计们，伙计们，伙计们”出场的时候吗？

409
00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:14.160
Michael, were you aware you were saying guys, guys, guys?
迈克尔，你意识到自己在说“伙计们，伙计们，伙计们”吗？

410
00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:16.020
Did you think of that as your own catchphrase?
你把这当成是你的招牌口头禅吗？

411
00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:18.060
Or did you only realize that was your catchphrase?
还是说你直到意识到这是你的口头禅？

412
00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.580
Once we started mocking you on air.
是在我们开始在节目里嘲笑你之后。

413
00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:23.180
Like, tell us the story of guys, guys, guys.
给我们讲讲“伙计们，伙计们，伙计们”的故事吧。

414
00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:25.680
Because we talk about guys, guys, guys fairly often on here.
因为我们在这儿经常谈论“伙计们，伙计们，伙计们”。

415
00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:30.160
Yes, the creativity would just get to a certain volume during production.
是的，在制作过程中，创意就会达到一定的声量。

416
00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:32.060
Creativity, very generous term.
创意，这个词真是太慷慨了。

417
00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.680
And everyone would be just talking at a certain level.
每个人都会在某个音量级别上说话。

418
00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.220
And I yelled out, guys, guys, guys.
然后我大喊，伙计们，伙计们，伙计们。

419
00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.600
And from then on, you know.
然后从那以后，你懂的。

420
00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:42.340
But you leaned into it.
但你顺水推舟了。

421
00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:44.560
You knew that you were branded as guys, guys, guys.
你知道自己被贴上了“伙计们，伙计们，伙计们”的标签。

422
00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:46.080
And then you would do it.
然后你就会这么做。

423
00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:47.480
And it would get a laugh every time.
而且每一次都能引来笑声。

424
00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:48.740
It was your, like, legendary.
这简直成了你的，传奇般的。

425
00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:49.800
That was your catchphrase.
那是你的口头禅。

426
00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:53.920
It was being a scold because it became a stock comedic catchphrase.
这就成了一种唠叨，因为它变成了一个大众的喜剧口头禅。

427
00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:57.400
But we flag it every time it happens, Michael, on the show.
但迈克尔，每当它出现时，我们在节目里都会标记出来。

428
00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:58.160
And it's a lot.
而且次数很多。

429
00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:03.160
When I watch the show with my son Hudson and Dylan, they go,
当我跟我儿子哈德逊和迪兰一起看节目时，他们会说，

430
00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.500
Oh, they just did guys, guys, guys.
哦，他们刚刚说了“伙计们，伙计们，伙计们”。

431
00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:09.320
It's like a mini him-yum drinking game.
这就像是一个迷你的老爸老妈浪漫史喝酒游戏。

432
00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:12.600
I mean, maybe this episode itself is going to have to be called guys, guys, guys.
我的意思是，说不定这一集本身就得叫做“伙计们，伙计们，伙计们”。

433
00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:16.980
But so, Michael, also, tell us about directing Intervention,
所以，迈克尔，还有，跟我们讲讲执导《干预》的情况吧，

434
00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:18.320
the episode we're talking about today.
也就是我们今天聊的这一集。

435
