a smaller, are there smaller uses for this?
更小规模的，有没有更小范围的用途？

1180
00:50:14.150 --> 00:50:17.270
It shows how hard it is to bring in a sixth, right?
这说明要引入第六个人有多难，对吧？

1181
00:50:17.430 --> 00:50:23.670
Like, like these people are really dialed in on their own mythology and their own, you
就像，这些人真的对他们自己的背景设定和他们自己的一套

1182
00:50:23.670 --> 00:50:25.170
know, secret coded language.
你知道的，秘密暗号般的语言非常投入。

1183
00:50:25.350 --> 00:50:25.610
Right.
没错。

1184
00:50:25.750 --> 00:50:26.630
Like you had to be there.
就好像你必须身临其境。

1185
00:50:26.750 --> 00:50:30.650
You had to go through the evolution of like doing this many, many times in our group.
你必须经历过我们这个团队一次又一次这么做演变过程。

1186
00:50:31.010 --> 00:50:32.250
And I love that.
我真的很喜欢这一点。

1187
00:50:32.250 --> 00:50:35.910
But I think that's, that's just how, how those are your best friends, right?
但我觉得，这正是，这就是你最好的朋友之间的相处方式，对吧？

1188
00:50:36.070 --> 00:50:39.890
When you devise your own language, like it's really like a little dialect you're creating.
当你设计自己的语言时，那真的就像你们在创造一种专属的小方言。

1189
00:50:40.010 --> 00:50:45.650
And even though most of the intervention stuff was played for laughs, it ultimately is a gesture
尽管大部分干预的桥段都是为了搞笑，但它归根结底是一个

1190
00:50:45.650 --> 00:50:49.270
of love, which is we're trying to save you from your own worst impulses.
充满爱的举动，也就是我们试图把你从你最糟糕的冲动中拯救出来。

1191
00:50:49.630 --> 00:50:50.010
Yes.
是的。

1192
00:50:50.150 --> 00:50:52.850
And that was important because like, we didn't want to seem like we're mocking interventions
这一点很重要，因为我们不想显得像是在嘲笑干预聚会

1193
00:50:52.850 --> 00:50:54.770
or mocking addiction issues or anything like that.
或是嘲笑成瘾问题之类的事情。

1194
00:50:54.890 --> 00:50:57.930
Like it was the idea that they went to this one and it really helped their friend.
关键在于他们参加过那次聚会，而且它确实帮助了他们的朋友。

1195
00:50:57.930 --> 00:51:03.190
And then they were like, maybe there are just more targeted, miniature uses of this idea.
然后他们就想，也许这个点子还可以有更具针对性、更迷你的用法。

1196
00:51:03.570 --> 00:51:07.430
And I remember like, we've never wanted to seem disrespectful, but I think because it
我记得，我们从来不想显得不尊重，但我觉得因为

1197
00:51:07.430 --> 00:51:10.950
was done with love and this group loves each other and it's silly.
这是出于爱意完成的，这个团队互相关爱，而且很搞笑。

1198
00:51:11.070 --> 00:51:13.110
And I think it works.
我觉得效果很好。

1199
00:51:13.150 --> 00:51:16.430
I've never, I've never, I've never heard anyone who was upset watching this episode.
我从来没有，从来没有，从来没有听谁说看这一集时感到不高兴。

1200
00:51:16.570 --> 00:51:16.890
Thank goodness.
谢天谢地。

1201
00:51:17.430 --> 00:51:19.210
But it definitely, that was the idea.
但这绝对，这就是当时的初衷。

1202
00:51:19.330 --> 00:51:20.150
They love each other.
他们彼此相爱。

1203
00:51:20.330 --> 00:51:24.890
And when everyone in the group decides you're one of the people in the group has gone off
当团里的每个人都觉得你们之中的某个人稍微有点

1204
00:51:24.890 --> 00:51:29.990
track a little bit and they want to be honest with them and find a format to honestly communicate
偏离了轨道，而他们又想对这个人坦诚相待，找到一种形式来坦率地沟通

1205
00:51:29.990 --> 00:51:32.070
something to this person that might not be working.
这个人身上可能有些行不通的地方。

1206
00:51:32.510 --> 00:51:34.990
And with Ted, there's a real emotional one in this episode.
而且对特德来说，这一集里有一个非常走心情节。

1207
00:51:35.190 --> 00:51:36.830
Should you be getting married to this woman?
你真的应该娶这个女人吗？

1208
00:51:36.950 --> 00:51:38.350
Is this, are you rushing into this too much?
这是，你是不是把这事办得太急了？

1209
00:51:38.790 --> 00:51:42.690
Like it's all done with love and protection and care.
就好像这一切都是出于爱、保护和关心。

1210
00:51:42.690 --> 00:51:47.930
But what's funny is we think you might be marrying the wrong woman and you have to stop
但搞笑的是，我们觉得你可能娶错了女人，而你必须停止

1211
00:51:47.930 --> 00:51:50.210
wearing those Crocs, get the same treatment.
穿那些洞洞鞋，享受同样的待遇。

1212
00:51:51.250 --> 00:51:52.590
And the same music cue.
还有同样的配乐。

1213
00:51:52.770 --> 00:51:55.070
The same music cue, the same solemnity.
同样的配乐，同样的庄严感。

1214
00:51:56.390 --> 00:51:58.350
That's the only way the bit works.
这才是这个梗能成立的唯一方式。

1215
00:51:58.530 --> 00:51:59.490
It's a great one.
这集太棒了。

1216
00:51:59.670 --> 00:52:00.670
It's a great episode.
这一集真精彩。

1217
00:52:00.950 --> 00:52:02.070
You're hilarious in it, Josh.
乔什，你在里面太搞笑了。

1218
